      "id": "efb15551-ba99-4088-a0e3-2f8562d164bf",
      "attributes": {
        "locale": "en-US",
        "whatsNew": "Alarms is now the fourth tab with a bell icon, and alarm management has moved out of Settings.\n\nTest notification permission: Enable notifications should show the iOS prompt; denied access should offer Open notification settings; the card should disappear after permission is allowed, including when returning from iOS Settings.\n\nLocal alarms use the grouped list with prominent times and date columns. Tap a saved alarm to edit its date/time with the same native picker used from pass details. Check that cancelling preserves the alarm, saving updates it in place, deleting removes it, and a scheduled local alarm plays the default notification sound on your device."
      },
